            <ArticleTitle>The Semaphorin 3E/PlexinD1 axis regulates macrophage inflammation in obesity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>461-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2013.09.011</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(13)00380-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Increased accumulation of adipose tissue macrophages in obesity propagates chronic inflammation that is closely associated with insulin resistance and type 2 diabetes. Semaphorin 3E, a guidance molecule for neurons, takes on a new role in obesity by directing the recruitment of macrophages in visceral adipose tissue (Shimizu et al., 2013).</AbstractText>
